Problem
Measure annual growth in new Airbnb hosts. Return signup_year, new_hosts, prev_year_hosts, and growth_pct, calculated as the percentage change from the preceding available year; the first year has empty comparison values. Sort by year.

Output columns: signup_year, new_hosts, prev_year_hosts, growth_pct


--- write SQL Query here
with yearly_host as 
(
    select 
        extract(year from signup_date)::INT as signup_year,
        count(*) as new_hosts
    from hosts
    group by extract(year from signup_year)
),
host_growth
order by as 
(
    select 
        signup_year,
        new_hosts
        lag(new_hosts, 1) over(order by signup_year asc) as prev_year_hosts
        from yearly_host
) 
select 
    signup_year;,
    new_hosts,
    prev_year_hosts,
    round(100.0*(new_hosts - prev_year_hosts)/nullif(prev_year_hosts, 0), 2) as growth_pct
    from host_growth
    order by signup_year;
